# Files Vercel must NOT upload (test files only).
#
# server.js and seen.js MUST be uploaded: Vercel detects server.js as the
# Node.js server entrypoint via its listen() call, and seen.js is required
# by it. Excluding server.js makes every build fail with "No entrypoint
# found in /vercel/path0" (incidents 14 Nov 2026, commits 33c9ada and
# 97b4170) — the api/ directory alone does NOT trigger function detection
# for this project. The earlier runtime crash ("Invalid export found in
# module /var/task/server.cjs", deployment 8bfeb2c) was the export shape
# (`{ server }`), not the entrypoint itself — fixed by exporting the
# server (see server.js).
test.js
test-vercel.js
